        is_verified=True,
        requirements=["Applications must be submitted through the Chevening online application system reached from your own country/territory page.", "Opt in to be considered for the Chevening SIDS Scholarship within the standard Chevening Scholarship application.", "Choose three different eligible UK master's degree courses in order of preference; duplicate courses at the same university cannot be considered.", "Courses must be full-time, taught master's courses (not research-focused MRes programmes), based in the UK, starting in the autumn term (usually September/October) and lasting nine to twelve months.", "Courses cannot be part-time, distance learning, a PhD or DPhil, or include more than one month of study outside the UK.", "Provide the names and contact details of two referees in the application.", "If shortlisted, upload two reference letters and your undergraduate degree certificate to the online application system no later than seven working days before your interview.", "If successful at interview, submit at least one unconditional UK university offer by 17:00 BST on 8 July 2027.", "Apply for your own student visa; Chevening cannot apply on your behalf."],
        selection_notes="Applications are sifted against the eligibility criteria from October 2026, then independent reading committees assess all eligible applications from mid-October 2026 to January 2027. British embassies and high commissions produce shortlists and interview candidates in March to April 2027; results are announced from mid-June 2027. Applicants are assessed on leadership and influencing skills, the ability to build professional relationships to achieve positive outcomes, the reasons for the course and university choice (linked to UK priorities such as promoting growth and prosperity, building climate resilience, strengthening security and stability, and supporting development for more inclusive and effective societies), and a realistic short, mid and long-term career plan. Chevening states: 'The use of AI software to generate answers in Chevening applications is strictly prohibited.' The official page does not publish a separate SIDS selection weighting, so the SIDS element appears to be applied alongside the standard Chevening assessment.",
