    ScholarshipIngestionRecord(
        name="Appel à projets M-ERA.NET 2026/27 - Science et ingénierie des matériaux pour l'innovation en Europe",
        country="France",
        degree_levels="Master's, PhD",
        funding_type="Partial",
        deadline="Annual cycle (check official website)",
        deadline_precision="varies",
        coverage=["Varies by programme"],
        official_source_url="https://anr.fr/fr/detail/call/appel-a-projets-m-eranet-202627-science-et-ingenierie-des-materiaux-pour-linnovation-en-europe",
        is_verified=True,
        requirements=["Pre-proposals and detailed proposals, written in English, must be deposited by the project coordinator on the M-ERA.NET Call 2026 submission site.", "Use of the templates available on the M-ERA.NET site is mandatory; any unauthorised modification, in particular exceeding the page limit, may render the proposal ineligible.", "The pre-proposal must be the duly completed pre-proposal form, in English, complying with the mandatory layout conditions.", "The detailed proposal must be the duly completed detailed-proposal form in English, complying with the mandatory layout conditions, and must include Annex 1 describing the Partner profiles together with the CVs of all consortium participants, also in English.", "Partners requesting ANR aid invited to step 2 must additionally deposit their detailed proposal on the ANR submission site, with information identical to the central deposit; the exact link and deadline are communicated later by email.", "National and regional eligibility, selection and funding rules apply at both steps, and for some countries/regions restrictions on topics, TRL levels and the type of eligible partners apply.", "The scientific and technological objectives stated in the pre-proposal cannot be modified at step 2.", "It is not possible to add Partners from new countries to the consortium in step 2; only new Partners from countries already involved in the pre-proposal via a funding request to one of their funding agencies may be added.", "Any change must be communicated to and accepted by the requested funding agencies and the call secretariat at least two weeks before the step 2 closing date, with the consortium coordinator ensuring acceptance.", "The scientific lead (Responsable scientifique) formally commits that their hierarchy (administrative and financial services and persons legally entitled to represent the managing institution, or their representatives) has approved the submission and that the information has been communicated to them.", "French project leaders (requesting funding or not) ensure compliance with the national research professions deontology charter and the ANR deontology and scientific-integrity charter within the research activities carried out under their responsibility.", "Where genetic resources are used, all participants (requesting funding or not) must respect the Nagoya Protocol obligations, and beneficiaries under the access-and-benefit-sharing regulation must provide the Due Diligence Declaration receipt by the date of the final payment.", "Where relevant, take into account the sex and/or gender dimension in the research and give equitable visibility to the work produced.", "Before any ANR project deposit, applicants should approach their institution's defence and security officer or PPST services to verify their project's eligibility conditions; projects with foreign public or private partners are subject to SHFDS/MESR opinion, and a negative opinion prevents selection."],
        selection_notes="Evaluation and selection are centralised at M-ERA.NET level and take place in two steps: step 1 central evaluation of pre-proposals by independent international experts convened by the M-ERA.NET Call Secretariat, with invitations to step 2 issued in ranking order and taking account of the participating agencies' budget capacity; step 2 central evaluation of detailed proposals by independent international experts convened by the same secretariat. Proposals are ranked on the evaluation results and selection follows the ranking. The list of projects recommended for funding is drawn up by the group of participating funders taking account of their respective budget capacities, and the final funding decision is then taken individually by the funders concerned. Results are sent by the call secretariat to the project coordinators. Evaluation modalities and criteria are those of the call text (Guide for proposers) available on the ANR call page and the M-ERA.NET call site; the ANR adds its own horizontal objectives, which are that projects show significant French participation (in coordination or in charge of a substantial part of the work), generate significant opening and diversification of French collaboration networks, and are ambitious with a clear intention of continuity and evolution of the collaboration. During discussions to separate projects of similar scientific quality within the funder group, projects involving a wider and/or more diverse consortium may be favoured.",
        program_type="Research grant",
        application_period="Ouverture : 31/03/2026 à 09:00 CEST. Limite de dépôt des pré-dossiers : 12/05/2026 à 12:00 CEST (step 1, closed). Limite de dépôt des projets : 18/11/2026 à 12:00 CET (step 2, open on 2026-10-01). An information webinar was held on 18 March 2026, 12:00-14:00 CET, with presentations and the recording available on the M-ERA.NET call site.",
        region="Europe",
        duration="Maximum project duration is 3 years (36 months).",
        catalogue_url="https://www.m-era.net/joint-calls/joint-call-2026",
        official_updates_url="https://anr.fr/fr/appels",
        preferred_id=318,
    ),
    ScholarshipIngestionRecord(
        name="France 2030 - PEPR GFM \"Grands Fonds Marins\" - Appel à projets - 2026",
        country="France",
        degree_levels="Master's, PhD",
        funding_type="Partial",
        deadline="Annual cycle (check official website)",
        deadline_precision="varies",
        coverage=["Varies by programme"],
        official_source_url="https://anr.fr/fr/france-2030/france2030/call/france-2030-pepr-gfm-grands-fonds-marins-appel-a-projets-2026",
        is_verified=True,
        requirements=["Obtain an account (login and password) on the ANR submission site in advance; the AAP recommends registering as early as possible.", "Deposit the complete submission file electronically from the project manager's account before the published closing date and time.", "Only the electronic version of the submission documents present on the submission site at the call closing time is taken into account for evaluation.", "Define, in the scientific document, a structured maturation phase at the start of the project, with duration, budget and responsible persons, producing an operational roadmap, an ethical issues analysis, an internal ethics charter and a Data Management Plan.", "Designate a person responsible for data (référent données) who drafts and updates the PGD.", "Identify, from the time of submission, a person responsible for ethical issues (référent des enjeux éthiques).", "Identify among the people involved in the project one person responsible for monitoring equity and inclusion (équité et inclusion).", "Describe strategies for maintaining the interdisciplinary and/or transdisciplinary dialogue throughout the project and designate the person responsible for monitoring them.", "Explicitly justify in the project budget the participation of project leaders in 2 in-person meetings every 18 months in metropolitan France and 3-4 travels for workpackage leaders or staff in training (doctorate or post-doctorate) every 2 years.", "Projects acquiring new data or samples at sea on unprogrammed French oceanographic fleet (IR* Flotte) means must justify why non-realisation would not undermine the project and must follow the upstream operational feasibility study procedure of the IR* Flotte (FOF naval operations pole); the minutes of the ad hoc commission (CNFH or CNFC) must be supplied.", "Data management must rely on the Research e-Infrastructures tools and services (Data-Terra, Huma-num, Progedo), following FAIR and, where relevant, CARE principles."],
        selection_notes="Only proposals satisfying the eligibility criteria (critères de recevabilité) are transmitted to the evaluation committee and can in no case be funded. Eligible projects are assessed by an independent international-dimension committee convened by the ANR, which may call on external experts and may hear project leaders (with project representatives) after sending questions in advance. The committee produces (1) a list of projects it recommends for funding on the published criteria and (2) a list it proposes not to fund because quality is insufficient on at least one criterion, with a written justification for each project, and may give an opinion on the amount requested. Uninvolved PEPR GFM programme directors then propose to the SGPI which projects could be financed and at what amount; the Prime Minister, after opinion of the CPMo and the SGPI, decides beneficiaries and amounts, and each project is covered by a contract between the ANR and the coordinating institution. Evaluation criteria fall into three groups: (a) scientific ambition and excellence (research question going beyond the documented state of the art, discipline combination justified by the question, dialogue of conceptual frameworks, ethical questions treated as integral to ambition); (b) quality of the consortium, resources mobilised and governance (recognised complementary expertise, adequacy of staff with objectives including a precise role and career benefit for each contractual worker, structured maturation phase, mechanisms for shared appropriation of questions, inventory/acquisition/management strategy for data and samples, recurrent ethical monitoring mechanisms, explicit choices to minimise the environmental footprint, coherent sizing with an argued 0.8-3 M€ budget); (c) fit with the PEPR GFM challenges and impact (clear fit with at least one challenge and the programme's strategic priorities, described scientific/economic/environmental/societal impacts, described sharing of data and results, open-access data strategy with FAIR and CARE and Opidor PGD links, dissemination to academic and non-academic audiences).",
        program_type="Research grant",
        application_period="Ouverture : 21/07/2026 à 09:00 CEST. Clôture : 17/11/2026 à 11:00 CET. Single-phase call (l'appel à projets se déroule en une seule phase): full proposals are submitted and evaluated by an international committee set up by the ANR.",
        region="Europe",
        duration="Projects must run between 36 and 54 months.",
        official_updates_url="https://anr.fr/fr/france-2030/appels",
        preferred_id=319,
    ),
    ScholarshipIngestionRecord(
        name="France 2030 - PEPR PROPSY - \"Psychiatrie de précision\" - Appel à projets - 2026",
        country="France",
        degree_levels="Master's, PhD",
        funding_type="Partial",
        deadline="Annual cycle (check official website)",
        deadline_precision="varies",
        coverage=["Varies by programme"],
        official_source_url="https://anr.fr/fr/france-2030/france2030/call/france-2030-pepr-propsy-psychiatrie-de-precision-appel-a-projets-2026",
        is_verified=True,
        requirements=["Open an account (login and password) on the ANR submission site in advance; the AAP recommends registering as early as possible.", "Deposit the complete submission file electronically from the project manager's account before the published closing date and time.", "Only the electronic version of the submission documents present on the submission site at the call closing time is taken into account for evaluation.", "Contribute to strengthening and enhancing the capacity of French research actors, their attractiveness, their European and international influence, and their impact on the economy and society.", "Produce high-quality research strengthening the acquisition of disciplinary and/or interdisciplinary scientific knowledge to address current and future precision-psychiatry issues.", "Valorise the research and innovation produced, accompanying clinical implementation and/or industrialisation.", "Integrate the sharing of data, results and knowledge in an open science logic.", "Respect the PROPSY thematic scope: projects mainly on addictions are not eligible, except where those conditions are addressed within precision psychiatry as secondary phenomena or comorbidities of one of the four PEPR PROPSY disorders.", "Integrate a humanities and social sciences dimension where relevant, for example analysis of care pathways, clinical, social or ethical acceptability of innovations, and/or the involvement of patients, affected persons or associations in the design, implementation and valorization of projects.", "Signal any overlap with an already funded or submitted project and supply, where applicable, the justifications showing the absence of duplication.", "Where relevant, rely on public or private co-funding, national or international: these are not mandatory but are encouraged.", "For clinical studies, the data sets mobilised (cohorts, national or international databases, SNDS or existing health data warehouse data) must be identified and documented from the submission to guarantee project feasibility within the granted duration.", "For clinical studies, included patients must present at least one disorder of interest to PEPR PROPSY (bipolar disorders, resistant depressions, psychotic disorders, autism spectrum disorders) and/or the project may cover several disorders simultaneously.", "For the pre-clinical axis, explicitly declare the co-deposit of the project or obtain agreement from the French and foreign partner institutions; the actual co-deposit wording is not published in the AAP for this axis, so confirm it with the ANR contact."],
        selection_notes="Only proposals meeting the eligibility criteria (critères de recevabilité) are transmitted to the evaluation committee and can in no case be funded. Eligible projects are evaluated by an independent international-dimension committee, which may use external experts and may hear project leaders (with project representatives) after transmitting questions in advance. The committee delivers to the PEPR PROPSY scientific directors a report with a list of projects recommended for funding, a list of projects it proposes not to fund for insufficient quality on at least one criterion, a written justification for every project, and possibly an opinion on the amounts requested. The PEPR PROPSY scientific directors then propose to the SGPI which projects could be financed and at what amount; the Prime Minister, after SGPI opinion, decides beneficiaries and amounts, and each project is covered by a contract between the ANR and the coordinating institution. Evaluation criteria fall into three groups: (1) excellence and scientific ambition in precision psychiatry - clarity of objectives and hypotheses, innovativeness, ambition, originality, methodological or conceptual rupture against the state of the art, methodological relevance, preliminary data, project feasibility; (2) quality of the consortium, project management, resources mobilised and governance - competence, expertise and involvement of the project leader including capacity to coordinate ambitious multidisciplinary projects or consortia, academic track record, international recognition, quality and complementarity of the scientific consortium, adequacy between human and financial means and the objectives, relevance of the schedule and management of scientific risks with alternative solutions and credible milestones, relevance and efficiency of governance including patient associations and links with industrial partners or other programmes; (3) impact and outcomes - capacity to address precision-psychiatry development issues, active strategy to measure economic and/or societal impact, contribution to solutions for pathophysiological, diagnostic or therapeutic issues, dissemination and valorization strategy in itinere and ex post, adherence to FAIR and Open Science principles and promotion of scientific culture. Committee members and external experts commit to ANR deontology and integrity rules, strict confidentiality, declaration of conflicts of interest, and a ban on AI tools in the evaluation.",
        program_type="Research grant",
        application_period="Ouverture : 24/06/2026 à 09:00 CEST. Fermeture : 10/11/2026 à 11:00 CET (extended from 15/10/2026). The call page shows status \"Ouvert – 2026\". A webinar was held on 26/08/2026 with presentation and FAQ published.",
        region="Europe",
        duration="24 to 48 months for the pre-clinical axis; 36 to 48 months for the clinical and mixed axes.",
        official_updates_url="https://anr.fr/fr/france-2030/appels",
        preferred_id=320,
    ),
